{
  "manifest_version": 1,
  "comment": "Vendor asset manifest (T-ARCH-04, per R6). Declares every third-party art pack staged into assets/vendor/: where it comes from, under which license, the exact files we keep, and the sha256 each staged file must hash to. Staging + verification + @2x pre-render: scripts/vendor_assets.gd (run via `make vendor-assets`). Downloading (--fetch mode): scripts/vendor_assets.sh. Files here are pipeline metadata, NOT game content — the game-facing side is content/mvp/art_manifest.tres (asset keys), validated by ContentValidator.",
  "render": {
    "method": "godot-image-load-svg-from-buffer",
    "scale": 2.0,
    "output_suffix": "@2x.png",
    "note": "Renderer decision of record: this machine has no Inkscape/rsvg-convert/ImageMagick and its ffmpeg lacks an SVG decoder (probed 2026-09-15). The R1-pinned vendored Godot 4.7.2-stable binary rasterizes SVGs deterministically via ThorVG (Image.load_svg_from_buffer), so the pipeline ships zero new dependencies and is reproducible by construction. Limitation (R6 documents it): ThorVG's SVG feature support is limited — complex vectors (gradients, filters, text elements) may render imperfectly. If fidelity issues appear when the Armorial pack lands, install Inkscape and add an inkscape renderer path before re-rendering."
  },
